    "llvm_signature": "void (ptr), flat address space, volatile exact-sized memory and byte alignment",
    "neverc_signature": "void __builtin_ia32_<operation><format>(void *); restores take const void *",
    "effects": "All forms are scheduling boundaries. FNSTENV masks exceptions; FNSAVE also initializes the FPU. Loads check incoming pending exceptions before the memory read and defer newly loaded exceptions until a waiting instruction. TOP/tag/payload replacement invalidates compiler FP/ST/MMX values.",
    "neverd": "Four append-only operand16 identities fix discarded short formats. Native LLVM calls and old-SDK assembly share image/effect ownership; both C routes share builtin selection and preserve FS/GS in assembly. Owned restore/operation/save remains one atomic context boundary."
  },
